# Git Coordination (complements docs/ANCHOR_PROTOCOL.md)

Repository: `https://github.com/svblab/HR-deck`

**ANCHOR_PROTOCOL.md remains authoritative** for branch naming, diff-first, ADR triggers, tests, and Definition of Done. This rule adds Git coordination safeguards so Cursor, humans, and LLM reviewers stay synchronized with GitHub.

Human-readable reference: `docs/CURSOR_GIT_COORDINATION.md`.

## Source of truth

- **`origin/master` is authoritative.** Never assume local `master` reflects GitHub.
- Before any branch, merge, rebase, PR, push, or sync decision:

```bash
git fetch --all --prune
git status --short --branch
git branch -vv
```

- Conversation history is **not** Git state. A commit existing is **not** proof its content is in `origin/master`.

## Three states (never say "done" alone)

| State | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **WORKING** | Local development on a dedicated branch; base SHA identified |
| **PR READY** | Pushed, PR exists, diff reviewed, DoD satisfied — **not merged** |
| **MERGED** | Intended content verified present in `origin/master` |

`PR READY` ≠ `MERGED`. CI green ≠ merged. Human said "I'll merge" ≠ merged.

## Verify merge by content

After squash/rebase merges, `merge-base --is-ancestor` may fail. Verify **content**:

```bash
git fetch origin --prune
git diff origin/master...HEAD   # before push
git show origin/master:<path>   # after reported merge
```

Question: *Does the expected content exist in `origin/master`?* — not *Does the original SHA exist?*

## Branch rules

- Follow naming in `docs/ANCHOR_PROTOCOL.md` (`epic/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `spike/`).
- Never develop on `master` unless explicitly authorized for repo-level emergencies.
- New work bases on verified `origin/master`, not stale local `master`:

```bash
git fetch origin
git switch master
git pull --ff-only origin master   # only when worktree is safe to update
git switch -c <branch> origin/master
```

- Stale local `master` is normal after human merges. **Never** push local `master` over `origin/master`. **Never** force-push `master`.

## Diff-first (before implement and before every push)

```bash
git diff --stat origin/master...HEAD
git diff origin/master...HEAD
git diff --check
git status
```

STOP and investigate: unrelated files, accidental reverts, EOL noise, generated files, stale-branch inheritance, unexpected deletions.

## Canonical workflow

```
VERIFY → DIFF → ACT → TEST → COMMIT → PUSH → PR READY
  → LLM REVIEW → (CHANGES REQUESTED → VERIFY) → APPROVED
  → HUMAN MERGE → VERIFY origin/master → MERGED
```

Cursor implements, commits, pushes, prepares/updates PR, reports Git state. **Cursor does not merge PRs** unless explicitly instructed.

After human reports merge: `git fetch --all --prune`, verify `origin/master`, then `git pull --ff-only origin master` before the next branch.

## Destructive operations — require explicit authorization

Never silently run:

```text
git reset --hard
git clean -fd
git push --force
git push --force-with-lease
git branch -D
git rebase
```

- **`[gone]` upstream does NOT mean safe to delete.** Verify no unique/unmerged commits first.
- Do not delete, stash, reset, or overwrite **untracked files** without authorization.

## Suspicious history — STOP and report

Do not auto-repair. Report:

```text
STOP — repository state inconsistency detected.
Expected: ...
Observed: ...
Likely cause: ...
No destructive Git operation was performed.
```

Triggers: orphan/unrelated `origin/master`, lost history, large unrelated revert, unexpected PR base, force-push, missing expected files/ADRs/EPICs.

## ADR

Evaluate ADR triggers per `docs/ANCHOR_PROTOCOL.md` §4 before implementation. Process-only Git coordination docs do not require an ADR by themselves.

## Required final report (PR work)

```text
## PR Status
PR: #<number>
Branch: <branch>
Base: origin/master @ <SHA>
HEAD: <SHA>
State: WORKING | PR READY | MERGED

## Diff
Files changed: <N> | Insertions: <N> | Deletions: <N>
Unrelated changes: none / <details>

## Tests
- <command> — PASS/FAIL
- CI — PASS/FAIL/PENDING

## Architecture
ADR impact: NONE / UPDATED / NEW ADR REQUIRED
EPIC impact: <list>

## DoD
- [x] ...

## Git Coordination
Remote checked at: origin/master @ <SHA>
Local master: <SHA>
Merge verified: YES / NO / NOT YET

## Next action
<exact next step for human or LLM>
```

Principle: **VERIFY → DIFF → ACT → VERIFY → REPORT** — not ASSUME → ACT → REPORT.
